      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "text": "Nodejs and Express Module:\n---------------------------\n\nNodejs :Node.js® is a free, open-source, cross-platform JavaScript runtime \nenvironment that lets developers create servers, web apps, command \nline tools and scripts.\n\nSo nodejs is just not a b runtime or javascript interpreter but \nit comes bundle with lot of pre built module/function which can be \nimported and used to make it much more easy to develop software without \ngetting it nitty gritty or writing everything from scratch \n\nunlike JavaScript browser runtime where we get webAPI in node js we have \nc++ api that is same async function built on c++ \n\n\nhttps://nodejs.org/en/learn/getting-started/introduction-to-nodejs\n\n\nHow to install Nodejs:\n1.goto https://nodejs.org/en ",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Nodejs and Express Module:\n---------------------------\n\nNodejs :Node.js® is a free, open-source, cross-platform JavaScript runtime \nenvironment that lets developers create servers, web apps, command \nline tools and scripts.\n\nSo nodejs is just not a b runtime or javascript interpreter but \nit comes bundle with lot of pre built module/function which can be \nimported and used to make it much more easy to develop software without \ngetting it nitty gritty or writing everything from scratch \n\nunlike JavaScript browser runtime where we get webAPI in node js we have \nc++ api that is same async function built on c++ \n\n\nhttps://nodejs.org/en/learn/getting-started/introduction-to-nodejs\n\n\nHow to install Nodejs:\n1.goto https://nodejs.org/en ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
