      "updated": 1729957862074,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "2.MJS(Module / Ecmascript module java-script)\n-----------------------------------------------\nMJS are new way to export and import module in js, \nThe .mjs extension in Node.js is used to indicate that a file is an ECMAScript Module (ESM). \nThis allows you to use import and export statements instead of the CommonJS require and module.exports.\n\n\nlets see how we can use them :\n-------------------------------\n1.create two file using .mjs extension:\n\n\n\n\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "2.MJS(Module / Ecmascript module java-script)\n-----------------------------------------------\nMJS are new way to export and import module in js, \nThe .mjs extension in Node.js is used to indicate that a file is an ECMAScript Module (ESM). \nThis allows you to use import and export statements instead of the CommonJS require and module.exports.\n\n\nlets see how we can use them :\n-------------------------------\n1.create two file using .mjs extension:\n\n\n\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
