      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1729960334789,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now one thing to notice is we use .mjs file extension in order to \nEcmaScript Module js ,well there is a other way around of it in \nwhich we can use it with simple .js file \n\n\nand that is using package.json\n\nWhat is a package.json it is a file which keeps the track of project \ndependencies name and version plus the type of js we will use that is \ncjs or mjs and using package.json we can use npm install to install all those \ndependencies listed in package.json with that perticular verion and when we \nrun node on our target file package.json will notify node to compile it \nusing mjs\n\n1.Create package.json file:\n\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now one thing to notice is we use .mjs file extension in order to \nEcmaScript Module js ,well there is a other way around of it in \nwhich we can use it with simple .js file \n\n\nand that is using package.json\n\nWhat is a package.json it is a file which keeps the track of project \ndependencies name and version plus the type of js we will use that is \ncjs or mjs and using package.json we can use npm install to install all those \ndependencies listed in package.json with that perticular verion and when we \nrun node on our target file package.json will notify node to compile it \nusing mjs\n\n1.Create package.json file:\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
