      "updated": 1729962106840,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Working of Node.js Behind the scene:\n\n->Now unlike a typical javascript file which we run in browser which get called on \na window object\n\na nodejs is a bit different when we type in a noraml code in nodejs what it does it wraps that code in \nmodule wrapper \n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Working of Node.js Behind the scene:\n\n->Now unlike a typical javascript file which we run in browser which get called on \na window object\n\na nodejs is a bit different when we type in a noraml code in nodejs what it does it wraps that code in \nmodule wrapper \n",
