    {
      "id": "H9MYXQFy76dDSR3J_yOeH",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1286.9268228205437,
      "y": 38811.67514760594,
      "width": 1504.79931640625,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bFy",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1001768515,
      "version": 441,
      "versionNonce": 1408800877,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1729991500483,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Note:__dirname is dependent on __filename so in order to use __dirname first\nimport fileURLToPath from \"url\" module which is a native nodejs module \nand then use fileURLToPath function on import.meta.url argument like:\nfileURLToPath(import.meta.url); to get back file path \n\nthen use __filname to get __dirname using dirname which is a function \nof path module",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Note:__dirname is dependent on __filename so in order to use __dirname first\nimport fileURLToPath from \"url\" module which is a native nodejs module \nand then use fileURLToPath function on import.meta.url argument like:\nfileURLToPath(import.meta.url); to get back file path \n\nthen use __filname to get __dirname using dirname which is a function \nof path module",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "VzjXMQLQ8rHf1Izlv7OuY",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1294.9016065543774,
      "y": 39433.708218002204,
      "width": 1603.799072265625,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bFz",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1591025965,
      "version": 429,
      "versionNonce": 284583117,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1729992008380,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Okay so in ESM or ES6 module syntax we got to know that __filename and __dirname \nare not present/available so in-order for us to replicate something similar \nin mjs we use fileURLToPath() which is a part of \"url\" module and dirname()\nwhich is part of \"path\" module \n\n\nso lets discuss what is path and url module:\n\n\n ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Okay so in ESM or ES6 module syntax we got to know that __filename and __dirname \nare not present/available so in-order for us to replicate something similar \nin mjs we use fileURLToPath() which is a part of \"url\" module and dirname()\nwhich is part of \"path\" module \n\n\nso lets discuss what is path and url module:\n\n\n ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
