      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730127365372,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now there are two type of stream :\n1.read stream\n2.write stream\n",
      "fontSize": 46.563184701715365,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now there are two type of stream :\n1.read stream\n2.write stream\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ne9lR76-lQwUZjfeZ2z76",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -1833.7557840792658,
      "y": 148129.11234644914,
      "width": 1960.39892578125,
      "height": 945,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bKj",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1041045091,
      "version": 660,
      "versionNonce": 362073485,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1730127682634,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "And we can see this in action using node fs module lets\n\nsee\n1.fs.createReadStream(fileName/filePath)\n\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\n\nconst readStream=fs.readStream(\"./large.txt\");\n\nreadStream.on(\"data\",(chunk)=>{\n    console.log(\"----NEW CHUNK----\");\n    console.log(chunk);\n})\n\nLets try to see what this code dies \nis \n\na)first we created a read stream using fs.readStream(\"./large.txt\") \nb)we added a event listner (.on) which gets triggered as soon as data from\nthat streams start comming and they get stored inside the buffer once a perticular buffer is filled\nit will log ",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "And we can see this in action using node fs module lets\n\nsee\n1.fs.createReadStream(fileName/filePath)\n\nimport fs from \"node:fs\";\n\nconst readStream=fs.readStream(\"./large.txt\");\n\nreadStream.on(\"data\",(chunk)=>{\n    console.log(\"----NEW CHUNK----\");\n    console.log(chunk);\n})\n\nLets try to see what this code dies \nis \n\na)first we created a read stream using fs.readStream(\"./large.txt\") \nb)we added a event listner (.on) which gets triggered as soon as data from\nthat streams start comming and they get stored inside the buffer once a perticular buffer is filled\nit will log ",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
